WEB8-015-001,CDC Laboratory Quality,standard,safety_guidance,general,4,general_safety;quality,What quality management elements are required to improve laboratory reliability,What quality management elements are required to improve laboratory reliability有哪些要点？,"Based on the referenced safety document 'CDC Laboratory Quality', this item requires risk-based controls for laboratory activities, including training access, containment conditions, PPE usage, waste control, and emergency response readiness. Applicable scenario: What quality management elements are required to improve laboratory reliability有哪些要点？. Key extracted context: December 6, 2024 CDC Enhances Laboratory Quality Overview CDC laboratories follow our pledge to produce the highest quality scientific data, while ensuring the safety of its staff and the nation. CDC Laboratory Worker Supporting CDC Laboratories in Laboratory Quality Efforts CDC laboratories conduct unique science and provide critical health information that protects the United States against dangerous health threats. High quality laboratory science is essential for CDC to meet its mission. Scientific data generated or supported by CDC’s laboratories forms the basis of critical public health decision making and policy. CDC has a responsibility to ensure that all CDC laboratory research and development activities, testing processes, and data are the highest quality possible and are traceable, reproducible, documented with appropriate rigor, and meet all applicable regulatory requirements. In 2019, CDC enacted an agency-wide laboratory quality management policy. This policy formalizes CDC’s commitment to scientific excellence and safety by establishing quality standard requirements for all CDC laboratories. Implementing this policy has further increased CDC’s core capability within i ...","1) Confirm the experiment scope, SOP, and approval requirements before operation.
