WEB7-001-001,CDC COVID-19 Laboratory Safety Resources,training,safety_guidance,biosafety,4,biosafety;general_safety,What laboratory biosafety controls are required for COVID-19 related specimen handling and testing,What laboratory biosafety controls are required for COVID-19 related specimen handling and testing有哪些要点？,"Based on the referenced safety document 'CDC COVID-19 Laboratory Safety Resources', this item requires risk-based controls for laboratory activities, including training access, containment conditions, PPE usage, waste control, and emergency response readiness. Applicable scenario: What laboratory biosafety controls are required for COVID-19 related specimen handling and testing有哪些要点？. Key extracted context: * This guidance is intended for clinical laboratory and support staff who handle or process specimens associated with COVID-19. * In December 2024, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) issued guidelines specifically for SARS-CoV-2. This revised guidance is specific to SARS-CoV-2 and should not be extrapolated to other members of the _Coronaviridae_ family or to other members of the species _Betacoronavirus pandemicum_. * Laboratories working with novel or emerging coronaviruses, such as those transmitted from animals to humans (e.g. new zoonotic coronaviruses), must evaluate the varying degrees of risk associated with coronaviruses. They should perform detailed risk assessments that take into account the specific location, the activities conducted, and the particular coronaviruses involved. []( ""Summary of recent changes"") ## Summary of recent changes Updates as of March 27, 2025: * Specified pathogens covered by the guidance View [previous updates]( []( ""Key points"") ## Key points * This guidance is intended for laboratory and support staff who handle or process SARS-CoV-2 samples such as clinical specimens, cultures, and environmental samples. * All laboratories s ...","1) Confirm the experiment scope, SOP, and approval requirements before operation.
2) Verify facilities (ventilation, containment, warning signs) and PPE readiness.
3) Execute operation with buddy-check, maintain records, and control exposure paths.
4) Handle samples/waste by classification and complete decontamination after use.
5) Report abnormalities immediately and trigger emergency response when needed.",lab coat; protective gloves; surgical mask or respirator,Do not perform high-risk procedures without training/authorization; do not bypass containment and engineering controls; do not operate alone in hazardous scenarios.,"Classify and package laboratory waste by hazard type, label clearly, and transfer through approved disposal workflow.","For exposure or injury, stop operation immediately, perform on-site first aid (flush/decontaminate/isolate), and seek medical support without delay.","Stop operation, isolate area, notify supervisor and EHS team, and execute the institutional emergency plan.",基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=jina；quality_score=0.6682。,CDC COVID-19 Laboratory Safety Resources | https://www.cdc.gov/covid/php/lab/index.html,网页,CDC COVID-19 Laboratory Safety Resources,CDC,,,https://www.cdc.gov/covid/php/lab/index.html,2026-03-29,,draft,cdc;covid-19;lab safety;auto_rewrite_low_quality,en
WEB7-002-001,OSHA Fact Sheet Laboratory Safety and the OSHA Laboratory Standard,standard,regulation,chemical,4,chemical;general_safety,What core compliance requirements are highlighted in the OSHA laboratory safety fact sheet,What core compliance requirements are highlighted in the OSHA laboratory safety fact sheet有哪些要点？,"Based on the referenced safety document 'OSHA Fact Sheet Laboratory Safety and the OSHA Laboratory Standard', this item requires risk-based controls for laboratory activities, including training access, containment conditions, PPE usage, waste control, and emergency response readiness. Applicable scenario: What core compliance requirements are highlighted in the OSHA laboratory safety fact sheet有哪些要点？. Key extracted context: O> SITX Fact Sheet # Laboratory Safety OSHA Laboratory Standard OSHA’s Occupational Exposure to Hazardous Chemicals in Laboratories standard (29 CFR 1910.1450), referred to as the Laboratory standard, covers laboratories where chemical manipulation generally involves small amounts of a limited variety of chemicals. This standard applies to all hazardous chemicals meeting the definition of “laboratory use” and having the potential for worker exposure. Hazardous chemicals present physical and/or health threats to workers in clinical, industrial, and academic laboratories. Hazardous laboratory chemicals include cancer-causing agents (carcino - gens), toxins that may affect the liver, kidney, or nervous system, irritants, corrosives, and sensitiz - ers, as well as agents that act on the blood system or damage the lungs, skin, eyes, or mucous membranes. OSHA rules limit all industry exposures to approximately 400 substances. Elements of the Laboratory Standard This standard applies to employers engaged in laboratory use of hazardous chemicals. 1 • “Laboratory” means a facility where the “labo - ratory use of hazardous chemicals” occurs. It is a workplace where relatively small quantitie ...","1) Confirm the experiment scope, SOP, and approval requirements before operation.
2) Verify facilities (ventilation, containment, warning signs) and PPE readiness.
3) Execute operation with buddy-check, maintain records, and control exposure paths.
4) Handle samples/waste by classification and complete decontamination after use.
5) Report abnormalities immediately and trigger emergency response when needed.",safety goggles; chemical-resistant gloves; lab coat,Do not perform high-risk procedures without training/authorization; do not bypass containment and engineering controls; do not operate alone in hazardous scenarios.,"Classify and package laboratory waste by hazard type, label clearly, and transfer through approved disposal workflow.","For exposure or injury, stop operation immediately, perform on-site first aid (flush/decontaminate/isolate), and seek medical support without delay.","Stop operation, isolate area, notify supervisor and EHS team, and execute the institutional emergency plan.",基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=jina；quality_score=0.6843。,OSHA Fact Sheet Laboratory Safety and the OSHA Laboratory Standard | https://www.osha.gov/sites/default/files/publications/OSHAFACTSHEET-LABORATORY-SAFETY-OSHA-LAB-STANDARD.pdf,网页,OSHA Fact Sheet Laboratory Safety and the OSHA Laboratory Standard,OSHA,,,https://www.osha.gov/sites/default/files/publications/OSHAFACTSHEET-LABORATORY-SAFETY-OSHA-LAB-STANDARD.pdf,2026-03-29,,draft,osha;fact sheet;laboratory standard;auto_rewrite_low_quality,en
