ُ (Arabic)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|ar"") ""Arabic"") * [Sinugbuanong Binisayâ (Cebuano)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|ceb"") ""Cebuano"") * [简体字 (Chinese-Simplified)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|zh-CN"") ""Chinese-Simplified"") * [繁体字 (Chinese-Traditional)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|zh-TW"") ""Chinese-Traditional"") * [English](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|en"") ""English"") * [Français (French)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|fr"") ""French"") * [Kreyòl ayisyen (Haitian Creole)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|ht"") ""Haitian Creole"") * [한국어 (Korean)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|ko"") ""Korean"") * [नेपाली (Nepali)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|ne"") ""Nepali"") * [Polski (Polish)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|pl"") ""Polish"") * [Português (Portuguese (Brazilian))](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|pt"") ""Portuguese (Brazilian)"") * [Русский (Russian)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|ru"") ""Russian"") * [Af-Soomaali (Somali)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|so"") ""Somali"") * [Español (Spanish)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|es"") ""Spanish"") * [Українська (Ukrainian)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|uk"") ""Ukrainian"") * [Tiếng Việt (Vietnamese)](javascript:doGTranslate(""en|vi"") ""Vietnamese"") * [Home](https://www.osha.gov/ ""Home"") * [Safety and Health Topics](https://www.osha.gov/topics/text-index ""Safety and Health Topics"") * Laboratories ### Laboratories [**Laboratories Menu**](https://www.osha.gov/laboratories/standards ""Laboratories Menu"")[**Workers' Rights**](https://www.osha.gov/workers/ ""Workers' Rights"") * [_Home_](https://www.osha.gov/laboratories ""Home"") * [Standards](https://www.osha.gov/laboratories/standards ""Standards"") * [Culture of Safety](https://www.osha.gov/laboratories/safety-culture ""Culture of Safety"") * [Enforcement](https://www.osha.gov/laboratories/enforcement ""Enforcement"") * [Hazard Recognition and Solutions](https://www.osha.gov/laboratories/hazard-recognition-solutions ""Hazard Recognition and Solutions"") * [Additional Resources](https://www.osha.gov/laboratories/resources ""Additional Resources"") * [Workers' Rights](https://www.osha.gov/workers ""Workers' Rights"") #### Standards There are several specific OSHA standards that apply to laboratories as well as other OSHA standards that apply to various aspects of laboratory activities. This section highlights OSHA standards and documents related to laboratories. ##### OSHA Standards General Industry (29 CFR 1910)| ##### **General Industry (29 CFR 1910)** | ##### **Related Information** | | --- | --- | | [1910 Subpart I](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910#1910_Subpart_I ""1910 Subpart I"") - Personal Protective Equipment | | [1910.132](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.132 ""1910.132""), General requirements. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.132 ""1910.132 Related Information"") | | [1910.133](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.133 ""1910.133""), Eye and face protection. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.133 ""1910.133 Related Information"") | | [1910.134](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.134 ""1910.134""), Respiratory protection. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.134 ""1910.134 Related Information"") | | [1910 Subpart J](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910#1910_Subpart_J ""1910 Subpart J"") - General Environmental Controls | | [1910.147](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.147 ""1910.147""), The control of hazardous energy (lockout/tagout). | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.147 ""1910.147 Related Information"") | | [1910 Subpart Z](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910#1910_Subpart_Z ""1910 Subpart Z"") - Toxic and Hazardous Substances | | [1910.1450](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1450 ""1910.1450""), Occupational exposure to hazardous chemicals in laboratories. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.1450 ""1910.1450 Related Information"") | | [1910.1200](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1200 ""1910.1200""), Hazard Communication. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.1200 ""1910.1200 Related Information"") | | [1910.1000](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1000 ""1910.1000""), Air contaminants. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.1000 ""1910.1000 Related Information"") | | [1910.1000 TABLE Z-1](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1000TABLEZ1 ""1910.1000 TABLE Z-1""), TABLE Z-1 Limits for Air Contaminants. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.1000%20TABLE%20Z-1 ""1910.1000%20TABLE%20Z-1 Related Information"") | | [1910.1048](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1048 ""1910.1048""), Formaldehyde. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.1048 ""1910.1048 Related Information"") | | [1910.1030](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1030 ""1910.1030""), Bloodborne pathogens. | [Related Information](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/interlinking/standards/1910.1030 ""1910.1030 Related Information"") | ##### State Plan Standards State Plans are OSHA-approved workplace safety and health programs operated by individual states or U.S. territories. Most State Plans cover both private sector and state and local government workers throughout the state, while several cover only state and local government workers. See a complete listing of all [State Plans](https://www.osha.gov/stateplans ""State Plans""). State Plans are required to have standards and enforcement programs that are at least as effective as OSHA's and may have different or more stringent requirements. [Explore specific State Plan safety and health standards and regulations](https://www.osha.gov/stateplans/statestandards ""Links to State Plans' Safety and Health Standards and Regulations""). ##### National Consensus Standards **Note:** These are NOT OSHA regulations. However, they do provide guidance from their originating organizations related to worker protection. _American National Standards Institute (ANSI)_ * _ANSI/American Industrial Hygiene Association (AIHA) - Z9_. Ventilation Package. The Ventilation Package establishes minimum control requirements and ventilation system design criteria for controlling and removing air contaminants. It particularly addresses airborne contaminants during open surface tank operations, laboratory ventilation and industrial process exhaust systems. This package contains all parts of ANSI/AIHA Z9. * ANSI Z9.5 – Laboratory ventilation. * ANSI Z9.11 – Laboratory decommissioning. * _ANSI/American Society of Heating, Refrigerating and Air-Conditioning Engineers (ASHRAE) 110_. Method of Testing the Performance of Laboratory Hoods. Specifies a quantitative test procedure for evaluation of a laboratory fume hood. A tracer gas is released at prescribed rates and positions in the hood and monitored in the breathing zone of a mannequin at the face of the hood. Based on the release rate of the tracer gas and average exposure to the mannequin, a performance rating is achieved. _National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) standards_ * _NFPA 45, Standard on Fire Protection for Laboratories Using Chemicals_. Applies to laboratories in which hazardous chemicals are handled or stored. [Scroll to Top](https://www.osha.gov/laboratories/standards#) * [OSHA](https://www.osha.gov/aboutosha ""OSHA"") * [Standards](https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs ""Standards"") * [Enforcem