ogical-risk-assessment/index.html)[Biorisk Management](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/biorisk-management/index.html)[ECHO Biosafety Program](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety/index.html)[ECHO Biosafety Program: 2023](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/index.html)[Trainings](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/biosafety-training/index.html)[Resources and Tools](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/resources-tools/index.html)[Town Hall Meeting](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/biosafety-town-hall/index.html)[View Menu](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/resources-tools/index.html#) ![Image 7](blob:http://localhost/06f2109113c3546565baf16868a92620) September 21, 2024 # Resources and Tools ## What to know Through, federal and state agencies, professional societies, and the Division of Laboratory System’s (DLS) work with other CDC programs international organizations, DLS supports the development and adoption of standards, guidelines, recommendations, and tools for improved quality and safety in clinical and public health laboratories. [](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/resources-tools/index.html ""Background"") ## Background The following are useful resources to establish or strengthen biosafety practices in a clinical or public health laboratory. The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), or the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) cannot attest to the accuracy of a non-federal site and the listing of non-federal resources and tools below does not constitute an endorsement by HHS or any of its employees of the sponsors of the information or products. [View Larger](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/resources-tools/index.html#)[Download](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/images/RA_Graphic1_v03.png) ![Image 8: Circular diagram showing steps in risk management: identify, evaluate, control, implement, review.](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/images/RA_Graphic1_v03.png) 5 Steps of the Risk Management Process Flowchart. Find DLS's new [biological risk management resource](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/biological-risk-assessment/index.html). [](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/resources-tools/index.html ""Laboratory Outreach Communication System (LOCS) Calls"") ## Laboratory Outreach Communication System (LOCS) Calls [Laboratory Outreach Communication System Calls](https://www.cdc.gov/locs/calls/index.html) LOCS Call Survey. Please scan the QR code or click this link to complete a short survey about CDC’s... [](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/resources-tools/index.html ""Laboratory Biosafety Guidance"") ## Laboratory Biosafety Guidance [Biological Risk Assessment Process](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/biological-risk-assessment/process.html) Guide to identifying and mitigating biological risks in laboratory settings. [Biosafety in Microbiological and Biomedical Laboratories (BMBL) 6th Edition](https://www.cdc.gov/labs/bmbl/index.html) Best practices for the safe conduct of work in biomedical and clinical laboratories. [Biosafety in Microbiological and Biomedical Laboratories (BMBL) 6th Edition, Appendix N—Clinical Laboratories (pages 529 – 543)](https://www.cdc.gov/labs/pdf/SF__19_308133-A_BMBL6_00-BOOK-WEB-final-3.pdf#page=557) SF__19_308133-A_BMBL6_00-BOOK-WEB-final-3 [Download](https://www.cdc.gov/labs/pdf/SF__19_308133-A_BMBL6_00-BOOK-WEB-final-3.pdf#page=557) [Download](https://www.cdc.gov/labs/pdf/SF__19_308133-A_BMBL6_00-BOOK-WEB-final-3.pdf#page=557) [Guidelines for Safe Work Practices in Human and Animal Medical Diagnostic Laboratories](https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/su6101a1.htm?s_cid=su6101a1_w) [Guidelines & Guidance Library](https://www.cdc.gov/infectioncontrol/guidelines/index.html) Library of infection control guidelines and recommendations for healthcare settings. [CDC/APHL Guidelines for Biosafety Laboratory Competency](https://absa.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/MMWRguidelinesBSLcomp.pdf) [Download](https://absa.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/MMWRguidelinesBSLcomp.pdf) [Download](https://absa.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/MMWRguidelinesBSLcomp.pdf) [NIH Laboratory Biosafety Guidance for Research with SARS-CoV-2 and IBC Requirements](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/biosafety-and-biosecurity-policy/interim-laboratory-biosafety-guidance-for-research-with-sars-cov-2-and-ibc-requirements-under-the-nih-guidelines/) [NIH FAQs to Lower Minimum Required Biosafety Containment Level for Research Subject to Guidelines](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/biosafety-and-biosecurity-policy/faqs-nih-osp-review-of-requests-to-lower-the-minimum-required-biosafety-containment-level-for-research-subject-to-the-nih-guidelines/) [APHL Risk Assessment Best Practices and Examples](https://www.aphl.org/programs/preparedness/Documents/APHL%20Risk%20Assessment%20Best%20Practices%20and%20Examples.pdf) [Download](https://www.aphl.org/programs/preparedness/Documents/APHL%20Risk%20Assessment%20Best%20Practices%20and%20Examples.pdf) [Download](https://www.aphl.org/programs/preparedness/Documents/APHL%20Risk%20Assessment%20Best%20Practices%20and%20Examples.pdf) [Introduction to Laboratory Risk Management (LRM)](https://www.cdc.gov/labtraining/training-courses/Introduction-to-Laboratory-Risk-Management.html) s:59:""s:51:""Office of Public Health Scientific Services (OPHSS)"";""; [Guidelines for Safe Work Practices in Human and Animal Medical Diagnostic Laboratories, MMWR 61(01)](https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/pdf/other/su6101.pdf) [Download](https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/pdf/other/su6101.pdf) [Download](https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/pdf/other/su6101.pdf) [ISO 35001 Laboratory biorisk management system for laboratories and other related organizations](https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso:35001:ed-1:v1:en) [CWA 15793 Laboratory biorisk management](https://internationalbiosafety.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/CWA-15793-English.pdf) [Download](https://internationalbiosafety.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/CWA-15793-English.pdf) [Download](https://internationalbiosaf