WEB7-006-001,CDC Strong Laboratory Safety Program,biosafety,safety_guidance,biosafety,4,biosafety;general_safety,What program elements define a strong laboratory safety management system according to CDC,What program elements define a strong laboratory safety management system according to CDC有哪些要点？,"Based on the referenced safety document 'CDC Strong Laboratory Safety Program', this item requires risk-based controls for laboratory activities, including training access, containment conditions, PPE usage, waste control, and emergency response readiness. Applicable scenario: What program elements define a strong laboratory safety management system according to CDC有哪些要点？. Key extracted context: CDC advances two coequal and interrelated priorities: to strengthen _safety_ and _scientific excellence_ of every CDC laboratory. The director for the Office of Laboratory Systems and Response is the senior official who serves as the single point of accountability for laboratory science and safety at CDC. ![Image 1: CDC Lab Worker]( []( ""Director for the Office of Laboratory Systems and Response"") ## Director for the Office of Laboratory Systems and Response ![Image 2: Reynolds M. Salerno, PhD]( Reynolds M. Salerno, PhD Learn more about Dr. Salerno on [CDC’s leadership page]( []( ""CDC Activities to Strengthen Safety and Scientific Excellence in CDC Laboratories"") ## CDC Activities to Strengthen Safety and Scientific Excellence in CDC Laboratories ### Overseeing Safety in CDC Laboratories CDC is committed to continually improving its culture of safety in its laboratories where transparency and accountability are valued; staff receive complete, comprehensive, and cutting-edge safety training; the safety of a procedure or project is considered before all else; and potential safety issues are quickly and openly addressed. ![Image 3: CDC Lab Worker]( CDC Lab Worker While working with da ...","1) Confirm the experiment scope, SOP, and approval requirements before operation.
2) Verify facilities (ventilation, containment, warning signs) and PPE readiness.
3) Execute operation with buddy-check, maintain records, and control exposure paths.
4) Handle samples/waste by classification and complete decontamination after use.
5) Report abnormalities immediately and trigger emergency response when needed.",lab coat; protective gloves; surgical mask or respirator,Do not perform high-risk procedures without training/authorization; do not bypass containment and engineering controls; do not operate alone in hazardous scenarios.,"Classify and package laboratory waste by hazard type, label clearly, and transfer through approved disposal workflow.","For exposure or injury, stop operation immediately, perform on-site first aid (flush/decontaminate/isolate), and seek medical support without delay.","Stop operation, isolate area, notify supervisor and EHS team, and execute the institutional emergency plan.",基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=jina；quality_score=0.697。,CDC Strong Laboratory Safety Program | https://www.cdc.gov/labs/strong-lab-safety/index.html,网页,CDC Strong Laboratory Safety Program,CDC,,,https://www.cdc.gov/labs/strong-lab-safety/index.html,2026-03-29,,draft,cdc;strong lab safety;program;auto_rewrite_low_quality,en
