/safety-training.php) * [Shipping of Biological Substances](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/healthcare-safety/shipping-of-biological-substances.php) * [Fire Safety](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/healthcare-safety/fire-safety.php) * [Chemical Safety](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/healthcare-safety/chemical-safety.php) * [Accident and Injury Reporting](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/_archive_october_2025/occupational-safety/Injury-Reporting.php) * [Policies, Permits, Resources](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/policies-permits-resources/index.php) * [SBU](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/policies-permits-resources/policies-and-procedures-sbu.php) * [Hospital](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/policies-permits-resources/policies-and-procedures-hospital.php) * [Permits](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/policies-permits-resources/permits.php) * [Environmental Health And Safety Management System](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/resources/sms/) * [News and Information](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/news-information.php) * [Training](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/training.php) [Home](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/)[Programs](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/programs/)[Laboratory Safety](https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/programs/laboratory-safety/) ![Image 3: icon of a lab beaker](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/_images/laboratory_safety_icon.png) **LABORATORY SAFETY** The Laboratory Safety program supports EH&S's [Mission](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/about-us/about.php) by providing guidance and support to researchers in order to identify and eliminate or reduce hazards, train personnel, and ensure compliance with local, state and federal regulations. There are many regulatory requirements that laboratories must comply with when working with biological, chemical and radiological materials and it is our task to help identify the appropriate regulations and support the lab in maintaining compliance with them. The Laboratory Safety program provides policies, procedures, training, guidance, and other information to assist research and teaching personnel to provide a safe and healthful environment in which to operate. [Laboratory Security](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/laboratory-safety/laboratory-security.php) [Laboratory Registration](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/laboratory-safety/laboratory-registration.php) [Laboratory Safety Inspection](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/laboratory-safety/laboratory-safety-inspection.php) [Biological Safety](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/laboratory-safety/biological-safety/index.php) [Chemical Safety](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/laboratory-safety/chemical-safety/index.php) [General Laboratory Safety](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/laboratory-safety/general-laboratory-safety.php) [Laboratory Equipment](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/laboratory-safety/laboratory-equipment.php) ![Image 4: headshot of christopher kuhlow](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/_images/program_contacts_kuhlow.png) ![Image 5: ehs emblem](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/environmental-health-and-safety/_images/program_contacts_headshot_missing.png) # BIOLOGICAL SAFETY OFFICER Chris Kuhlow | (631) 632-3717 | Christopher.Kuhlow@stonybrook.edu # CHEMICAL HYGIENE OFFICER Ying Liu | (631) 632-3032 | Ying.Liu.1@stonybrook.edu [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/sbu.erm/ ""Connect with us on Facebook!"")[Twitter](https://twitter.com/sbu_erm ""Check out our latest Tweets!"")[instagram](https://www.instagram.com/sbu_erm/ ""Find us on Instagram!"")[linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/company/sbu-erm/ ""Connect on LinkedIn!"")[print](javascript:window.print() ""Print this page"") Division of Enterprise Risk Management Environmental Health & Safety 110 Suffolk Hall Stony Brook, NY 11794-6200 Phone: (631) 632-6410 Fax: 631-632-9683 [EHSafety@stonybrook.edu](mailto:EHSafety@stonybrook.edu) **We Care About...** Safety, People, Science, Education, Medicine and the Environment * [Discrimination](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/oea-equity/resources/complaint_intake_form.php) * [Sexual Misconduct](https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/oea-sm-tix/resources/titleix_initial_report.php) * [Accessibility Barrier](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScW_Uc4kfzvlKlgwoJCHSJ2EG_6bd-LjcHowxnNGKV0309uxg/viewform) [©Admin Login](http://a.cms.omniupdate.com/10?skin=oucampus&account=suny-stonybrook&site=sbcms&action=de&path=/environmental-health-and-safety/programs/laboratory-safety/index.pcf)2026[Stony Brook University](https://www.stonybrook.edu/)",,,,,,,基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=jina；quality_score=0.7392。,Stony Brook Laboratory Safety Program | https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/programs/laboratory-safety,网页,Stony Brook Laboratory Safety Program,Stony Brook University EHS,,,https://ehs.stonybrook.edu/programs/laboratory-safety,2026-03-29,,draft,stonybrook;laboratory safety;ehs,en
WEB6-001-001,NIOSH Pocket Guide to Chemical Hazards,chemical,safety_guidance,chemical,5,chemical;hazardous_chemicals,How can lab users apply NIOSH pocket guide limits and controls in daily operations,How can lab users apply NIOSH pocket guide limits and controls in daily operations有哪些要点？,"Title: Pocket Guide to Chemical Hazards | NIOSH URL Source: https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/default.html Markdown Content: # Pocket Guide to Chemical Hazards | NIOSH | CDC [Skip directly to site content](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/default.html#content)[Skip directly to search](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/default.html#headerSearch) [Español](https://www.cdc.gov/spanish/) | [Other Languages](https://wwwn.cdc.gov/pubs/other-languages/) ![Image 1](https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/4.0/assets/imgs/uswds/us_flag_small.png)An official website of the United States government Here's how you know ![Image 2](https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/4.0/assets/imgs/uswds/icon-dot-gov.svg) **Official websites use .gov** A .gov website belongs to an official government organization in the United States. ![Image 3](https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/4.0/assets/imgs/uswds/icon-https.svg) **Secure .gov websites use HTTPS** A lock ( ) or https:// means you've safely connected to the .gov website. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. [Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. CDC twenty four seven. Saving Lives, Protecting People![Image 4: CDC Logo](https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/4.0/assets/imgs/logo/logo-notext.svg)![Image 5: CDC Logo](https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/4.0/assets/imgs/logo/logo-notext.svg)](https://www.cdc.gov/) Search ×NIOSH [NIOSH](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/default.html#)[All CDC](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/default.html#) Submit [The National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health (NIOSH)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/) [![Image 6: NIOSH logo and tagline](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/images/si-no-left-vp4.png?_=94662)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/) # NIOSH Pocket Guide to Chemical Hazards [Print](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/default.html#print) [](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/default.html#collapse_2013769a5e0c900b5e) Related Pages ![Image 7: NIOSH Pocket Guide Cover](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/imageswcms/SilverNPGCover.png?_=78134) ## Overview The _NIOSH Pocket Guide to Chemical Hazards_ (NPG) informs workers, employers, and occupational health professionals about workplace chemicals and their hazards. The NPG gives general industrial hygiene information for hundreds of chemicals/classes. The NPG clearly presents key data for chemicals or substance groupings (such as cyanides, fluorides, manganese compounds) that are found in workplaces. The guide offers key facts, but does not give all relevant data. The NPG helps users recognize and control workplace chemical hazards. NIOSH offers four versions of the NPG: print, online, PDF, and mobile web app. Search the _Online NIOSH Pocket Guide to Chemical Hazards_ Enter search terms separated by spaces. For chemicals not listed and/or lacking occupational exposure limits (OELs), NIOSH recommends consulting the [NIOSH Occupational Exposure Banding Safety and Health Topic Page.](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/topics/oeb/default.html) [Index of Chemical Names, Synonyms and Trade Names](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/npgsyn-a.html) [Index of CAS Numbers](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/npgdcas.html) ### **Download the _NIOSH Pocket Guide to Chemical Hazards_ (mNPG)** [PDF Version The PDF version of the NPG is 6,192KB](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/docs/2005-149/default.html) [Mobile App The NIOSH Pocket Guide Mobile Web App requires an Apple iPhone or Android phone.](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/mobilepocketguide.html) [More Downloadable Versions](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/downloadable.html) Contents * [Introduction](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/pgintrod.html) * [Search the NIOSH Pocket Guide](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/search.html) * [Index of Chemical Names, Synonyms and Trade Names](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/npgsyn-a.html) * [Index of CAS Numbers](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/npgdcas.html) * [Index of RTECS Numbers](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/npgdrtec.html) * [Appendices](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/nengapdx.html) What's Inside The NIOSH Pocket Guide includes the following: * Chemical names, synonyms, trade names, CAS, RTECS, and DOT ID and guide numbers * Chemical structure/formula, conversion factors * NIOSH recommended exposure limits (RELs) * Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) permissible exposure limits (PELs) * [NIOSH immediately dangerous to life and health values (IDLHs)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/idlh/intridl4.html) * Physical description and chemical and physical properties of agents * Measurement methods * Personal protection and sanitation recommendations * Respirator selection recommendations * Incompatibilities and reactivities of agents * Exposure routes, symptoms, target organs, and first aid information Ordering Information **To order** free copies of the NIOSH Pocket Guide go to the [NIOSH document listing at CDC-INFO On Demand](https://wwwn.cdc.gov/pubs/CDCInfoOnDemand.aspx?ProgramID=147). **Other vendors** of the NIOSH Pocket Guide: [Superintendent of Documents](https://bookstore.gpo.gov/products/sku/017-033-00500-1) Government Printing Office Washington, D.C. 20402-9325 202-512-1800 GPO stock number 017-033-00500-1 [National Technical Information Service (NTIS)](https://ntrl.ntis.gov/NTRL/) National Technical Reports Library 5301 Shawnee Road Alexandria, VA 22312 Order Desk Telephone: (703) 605-6000 or 1-800-553-6847 NTIS order number PB2009103456 (only available as PDF download) [Contact CDC-INFO](https://www.cdc.gov/cdc-info/requestform.html) Last Reviewed: February 18, 2020 Source: [National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/) * [Facebook](https://api.addthis.com/oexchange/0.8/forward/facebook/offer?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cdc.gov%2F