www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/#collapse_1926166e1ef4b0ebfe) Related Pages [![Image 9: NIOSH Manual of Analytical Methods logo](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/images/NMAM-Logo200.jpg?_=77639)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/default.html) NMAM is a collection of sampling and analytical methods for workplace exposure monitoring. It includes methods for workplace air, surfaces, and blood and urine. NMAM includes chapters on method evaluation, sampling, and more. NIOSH or its partners have developed or adapted the methods included in the NMAM. NIOSH evaluates the methods according to established protocols and performance criteria. NIOSH recommends using the best method available for making each measurement. Other published methods may have advantages over NIOSH methods for a given sampling situation. Other potential method sources include: * [OSHA](http://www.osha.gov/) * [MSHA](http://www.msha.gov/) * [EPA](http://www.epa.gov/) * [ASTM](http://www.astm.org/) * [ISO](http://www.iso.ch/) * Commercial suppliers of sampling and analytical equipment An Industrial Hygienist should determine the sampling protocol, considering analytical accuracy, cost, and optimum sample number. Every method should undergo an initial evaluation to demonstrate performance. When using a method in a laboratory that did not perform the initial evaluation, verify it is possible to obtain comparable results. NIOSH methods may need modification. If modified, users should re-evaluate the method. For example, various[OSHA regulations](http://www.osha.gov/pls/oshaweb/owadisp.show_document?p_id=12716&p_table=standards)(e.g. benzene) mention performance criteria for evaluating the chosen method. Not all 4 th edition NIOSH methods are in the NMAM 5 th edition. This fact does not indicate that 4 th edition NMAM methods are invalid or not supported. It is simply an indication of where our limited resources have focused. Unless marked otherwise, NMAM 4 th edition methods are valid and supported. Remember, the NMAM 5 th edition is a living document that is updated as new or revised methods and chapters are ready for publication. In the Find a Method section below, NMAM 5 th edition methods can be found by Chemical Name, Chemical CAS Number, or Method Number. We’ve introduced a new search box that allows you to find methods from both the 4th and 5th editions of NMAM using various keywords, such as analyte, instrumentation, and sampler. You can also filter the search results by edition if needed. ![Image 10](https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/4.0/assets/imgs/left.png) [![Image 11: Updated NMAM Guidance Chapter FI: Measurement & Characterization of Fibrous Particles in Workplace Atmospheres](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/images/fiber-banner-2.jpg)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/pdf/Chapter-FI-Measurement-and-Characterization-of-Fibrous-Particle-in-Workplace-Atmospheres.pdf)[![Image 12: NMAM Method 6011: BROMINE and CHLORINE](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/images/6011banner.jpg)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/pdf/6011.pdf)[![Image 13: a beaker next to the text New NMAM search available - search the NMAM 4th and 5th editions at the same time! Check it out below!](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/images/NMAM-search.png) NMAM-search](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/#nmam-search)[![Image 14: new am chapter](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/images/Dustiness-chapter-image.png)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/pdf/Chapter-AD.pdf)[![Image 15: Issue 7908](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/images/7908_Image.png)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/docs/2014-151/pdfs/methods/7908_Issue2.pdf)[![Image 16: Image of biological samples, urine and blood.](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/images/BI-chapter-banner.jpg)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/pdf/Chapter-BI.pdf)[![Image 17: slide with image of surface sampling announcing publication of surface sampling chapter](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/images/SG-chapter-banner-3.jpg)](https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/nmam/pdf/NMAM_Chap_SG-508.pdf)[![Image 18: Chrysotile banne