WEB6-005-001,NIH Guidelines for Research Involving Recombinant or Synthetic Nucleic Acid Molecules,biosafety,national_standard,biosafety,5,biosafety;general_safety,What biosafety and governance obligations are required by the NIH recombinant DNA guidelines,What biosafety and governance obligations are required by the NIH recombinant DNA guidelines有哪些要点？,"Title: NIH Guidelines: Honoring the Past, Charting the Future URL Source: https://osp.od.nih.gov/biotechnology/nih-guidelines/ Markdown Content: # NIH Guidelines: Honoring the Past, Charting the Future - Office of Science Policy _Because of a lapse in government funding, the information on this website may not be up to date, transactions submitted via the website may not be processed, and the agency may not be able to respond to inquiries until appropriations are enacted. The NIH Clinical Center (the research hospital of NIH) is open. For more details about its operating status, please visit_[_cc.nih.gov_](http://cc.nih.gov/)_. Updates regarding government operating status and resumption of normal operations can be found at_[_opm.gov_](https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/snow-dismissal-procedures/current-status/)_._ ✕ [Skip to content](https://osp.od.nih.gov/biotechnology/nih-guidelines/#primary) [![Image 1: logo](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/OSP-logo.png)](https://osp.od.nih.gov/) [Office of Science Policy](https://osp.od.nih.gov/) Search Search for: Search for: * [About Us](https://osp.od.nih.gov/about-us/) * [News & Announcements](https://osp.od.nih.gov/category/announcements/) * [Policy Areas](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policy-areas/) * [Artificial Intelligence](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/artificial-intelligence/) * [Clinical Research](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/clinical-research/) * [Scientific Data Sharing](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/scientific-data-management-policy/) * [Biosafety and Biosecurity](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/biosafety-and-biosecurity-policy/) * [Public Access](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/public-access/) * [Bioethics in Research](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/bioethics-in-research/) * [Healthcare Research](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/healthcare-research/) * [Collaboration and Partnerships](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/collaboration-and-partnerships/) * [Stem Cell and Developmental Biology](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/stem-cell-and-developmental-biology-policy/) * [Advisory Committee Activities](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policy-areas/advisory-committee-activities/) * [Innovation and Translation](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/innovation-and-translation/) * [Return of Research Results](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/return-of-research-results/) * [Under the Poliscope Blog](https://osp.od.nih.gov/blog/) [Get Involved](https://osp.od.nih.gov/get-involved/) # Events & Meetings [Home](https://osp.od.nih.gov/) » [Events](https://osp.od.nih.gov/events/) » NIH Guidelines: Honoring the Past, Charting the Future # NIH Guidelines: Honoring the Past, Charting the Future **Event Date:** 07/18/2017 - 07/19/2017 **Time:** 8:30 am – 1:00 pm **Location:** 5701 Marinelli Rd North Bethesda, MD 20852 Share: [![Image 2: LinkedIn](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/themes/nih-osp-theme/dist/images/linkedin.png)](https://osp.od.nih.gov/#linkedin ""LinkedIn"")[![Image 3: Twitter](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/themes/nih-osp-theme/dist/images/twitter.png)](https://osp.od.nih.gov/#twitter ""Twitter"")[Share](https://www.addtoany.com/share#url=https%3A%2F%2Fosp.od.nih.gov%2Fevents%2Fnih-guidelines-honoring-the-past-charting-the-future%2F&title=NIH%20Guidelines%3A%20Honoring%20the%20Past%2C%20Charting%20the%20Future) On July 18-19, 2017, the NIH Office of Science Policy held a workshop on the NIH Guidelines for Research Involving Recombinant or Synthetic Nucleic Acid Molecules. The goals of the workshop were to examine the current biosafety oversight framework, and discuss the future direction of biosafety oversight in light of the emergence of new technologies in the life sciences and the evolution in our understanding of risk and safety. Questions about the workshop may be sent to[NIHGuidelines@od.nih.gov](mailto:NIHGuidelines@od.nih.gov). [Agenda](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/NIH_Guidelines_Workshop_Agenda.pdf) [Asilomar ’75: The Beginning of the Future](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g23oM-VqT_M) A retrospective video from some of the participants of the landmark “International Congress on Recombinant DNA Molecules” (aka Asilomar Conference) regarding the legacy of that historical event. #### Slides [Welcome and Introduction](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Welcome_and_Introduction.pdf) [Session I – David Baltimore, Ph.D.](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Session_I_Keynote_Baltimore.pdf) [Session II – Jessica Tucker, Ph.D.](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Session_II_Talk_Tucker.pdf) [Session II – Stephen J. Libby, Ph.D.](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Session_II_Talk_Libby.pdf) [Session II – Hans-Peter Kiem, M.D., Ph.D.](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Session_II_Talk_Kiem.pdf) [Session III – Deborah E. Wilson, RADM, DrPH, CBSP](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Session_III_Talk_Wilson.pdf) [Session III – Samuel Edwin, Ph.D.](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Session_III_Talk_Edwin.pdf) [Session III – Thomas Nerad, MPH, Ph.D.](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Session_III_Talk_Nerad.pdf) [Session IV – Zach Adelman, Ph.D](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Session_IV_Talk_Adelman.pdf). #### Webcasts Attendees may view the meeting remotely by visiting[www.videocast.nih.gov](http://www.videocast.nih.gov/), or clicking on the links below: **Day 1:**[https://videocast.nih.gov/summary.asp?live=24762&bhcp=1](https://videocast.nih.gov/summary.asp?live=24762&bhcp=1) **Day 2:**[https://videocast.nih.gov/summary.asp?live=24766&bhcp=1](https://videocast.nih.gov/summary.asp?live=24766&bhcp=1) [Close](https://osp.od.nih.gov/biotechnology/nih-guidelines/) ## Recent Events ##### Webinar on Modernizing the NIH Data and Safety Monitoring Policy 05/13/2026 To enhance efficiency and rigor, NIH intends to modernize the... [Read More](https://osp.od.nih.gov/events/webinar-on-modernizing-the-nih-data-and-safety-monitoring-policy/ ""Webinar on Modernizing the NIH Data and Safety Monitoring Policy"") ##### Development of a Draft NIH Policy for Responsibly Sharing Summary Level Study Results With Participants in NIH-Funded Clinical Research 04/27/2026 NIH is undertaking a comprehensive policy development process that will... [Read More](https://osp.od.nih.gov/events/development-of-a-draft-nih-policy-for-responsibly-sharing-summary-level-study-results-with-participants-in-nih-funded-clinical-research/ ""Development of a Draft NIH Policy for Responsibly Sharing Summary Level Study Results With Participants in NIH-Funded Clinical Research"") ##### Strengthening and Modernizing Biosafety Oversight: Region 6 Listening Session 02/26/2026 NIH, with the University of California Biological Safety Officer’s Working... [Read More](https://osp.od.nih.gov/events/strengthening-and-modernizing-biosafety-oversight-region-6-listening-session/ ""Strengthening and Modernizing Biosafety Oversight: Region 6 Listening Session"") Last updated: March 2025 ##### ABOUT US * [Meet the Senior Leadership Team](https://osp.od.nih.gov/about-us/leadership) * [Mission Statement](https://osp.od.nih.gov/about-us/#our-mission) * [Under the Poliscope Blog](https://osp.od.nih.gov/category/blog/) * [OSP Employee Directory](https://osp.od.nih.gov/about-us/directory/) * [OSP Staff Publications](https://osp.od.nih.gov/resources/) * [HHS Vulnerability Disclosure](https://www.hhs.gov/vulnerability-disclosure-policy/index.html) ##### POLICY AREAS * [Artificial Intelligence](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/artificial-intelligence/) * [Clinical Research](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/clinical-research/) * [Scientific Data Sharing](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/scientific-data-management-policy/) * [Biosafety and Biosecurity Policy](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/biosafety-and-biosecurity-policy/) * [Public Access](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/public-access/) * [Bioethics in Research](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/bioethics-in-research/) * [Healthcare Research](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/healthcare-research/) * [Stem Cell and Developmental Biology Policy](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/stem-cell-and-developmental-biology-policy/) * [Collaboration and Partnerships](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/collaboration-and-partnerships/) * [Advisory Committee Activities](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policy-area/advisory-committee-activities/) * [Innovation and Translation](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/innovation-and-translation/) * [Return of Research Results](https://osp.od.nih.gov/policies/return-of-research-results/) ##### MEETINGS AND EVENTS * [Recent & Upcoming Meetings](https://osp.od.nih.gov/events) ##### CONNECT WITH US [![Image 4: Twitter icon](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/themes/nih-osp-theme/dist/images/twitter.svg)](https://twitter.com/NIH_OSP)[![Image 5: LinkedIn icon](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/themes/nih-osp-theme/dist/images/linkedIn.svg)](https://www.linkedin.com/company/nih-office-of-science-policy/)[![Image 6: YouTube icon](https://osp.od.nih.gov/wp-content/themes/nih-osp-theme/dist/images/youtube.svg)](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UClLO4iMAvv2LIQDdAqtLs1Q) ##### USA.GOV * [Disclaimer](https://osp.od.nih.gov/disclaimer/) * [Accessibility](https://osp.od.nih.gov/accessibility-policy/) * [Web Privacy Notice](https://osp.od.nih.gov/web-privacy-notice/) * [NIH FOIA](https://www.nih.gov/institutes-nih/nih-office-director/office-communications-public-liaison/freedom-information-act-office) * [Get Acrobat Reader](http://get.adobe.com/reader/) ✓ Thanks for sharing! [AddToAny](https://www.addtoany.com/ ""Share Buttons"") [More…](https://osp.od.nih.gov/biotechnology/nih-guidelines/#addtoany ""Show all"")",,,,,,,基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=jina；quality_score=0.7522。,NIH Guidelines for Research Involving Recombinant or Synthetic Nucleic Acid Molecules | https://osp.od.nih.gov/biotechnology/nih-guidelines/,网页,NIH Guidelines for Research Involving Recombinant or Synthetic Nucleic Acid Molecules,NIH Office of Science Policy,,,https://osp.od.nih.gov/biotechnology/nih-guidelines/,2026-03-29,,draft,nih;rdna;biosafety,en
WEB6-006-001,Canadian Biosafety Standard Third Edition,biosafety,national_standard,biosafety,5,biosafety;general_safety,What mandatory biosafety program elements are required by the Canadian biosafety standard,What mandatory biosafety program elements are required by the Canadian biosafety standard有哪些要点？,"Based on the referenced safety document 'Canadian Biosafety Standard Third Edition', this item requires risk-based controls for laboratory activities, including training access, containment conditions, PPE usage, waste control, and emergency response readiness. Applicable scenario: What mandatory biosafety program elements are required by the Canadian biosafety standard有哪些要点？. Key extracted context: ## [Access the Biosecurity Addendum to the Canadian Biosafety Standard, Third Edition]( ## Table of contents * [Preface]( * [Abbreviations and acronyms]( * [Glossary]( * [1. Introduction]( * [1.1 Scope]( * [1.2 Regulatory authorities]( * [1.3 Working with human and animal pathogens and toxins]( * [1.4 Work activities]( * [2. How to use the _Canadian Biosafety Standard, Third Edition_]( * [2.1 Abbreviations, definitions and references]( * [2.2 Matrix layout: Sections 3, 4 and 5]( * [2.3 Explanatory notes]( * [2.4 _Canadian Biosafety Handbook_]( * [3. Physical containment requirements]( * [3.1 Containment barrier]( * [3.2 Access]( * [3.3 Surface finishes and casework]( * [3.4 Air handling]( * [3.5 Facility and services]( * [3.6 Essential biosafety equipment]( * [3.7 Effluent decontamination systems]( * [4. Operational practice requirements]( * [4.1 Biosafety program management]( * [4.2 Training program]( * [4.3 Personal protective equipment]( * [4.4 Entry and exit]( * [4.5 Work practices]( * [4.6 Animal work considerations]( * [4.7 Decontamination and waste management]( * [4.8 Emergency response]( * [4.9 Records and documentation]( * [5. Performance and verification testing requireme ...","1) Confirm the experiment scope, SOP, and approval requirements before operation.
2) Verify facilities (ventilation, containment, warning signs) and PPE readiness.
3) Execute operation with buddy-check, maintain records, and control exposure paths.
4) Handle samples/waste by classification and complete decontamination after use.
5) Report abnormalities immediately and trigger emergency response when needed.",lab coat; protective gloves; surgical mask or respirator,Do not perform high-risk procedures without training/authorization; do not bypass containment and engineering controls; do not operate alone in hazardous scenarios.,"Classify and package laboratory waste by hazard type, label clearly, and transfer through approved disposal workflow.","For exposure or injury, stop operation immediately, perform on-site first aid (flush/decontaminate/isolate), and seek medical support without delay.","Stop operation, isolate area, notify supervisor and EHS team, and execute the institutional emergency plan.",基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=jina；quality_score=0.6839。,Canadian Biosafety Standard Third Edition | https://www.canada.ca/en/public-health/services/canadian-biosafety-standards-guidelines/third-edition.html,网页,Canadian Biosafety Standard Third Edition,Public Health Agency of Canada,,,https://www.canada.ca/en/public-health/services/canadian-biosafety-standards-guidelines/third-edition.html,2026-03-29,,draft,canada;biosafety standard;phac;auto_rewrite_low_quality,en
